Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a legacy compact carrying another account's native
 compaction is refused here, saying why, not relayed to be refused there
 (#2642)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed:
- codexBackend's /responses/compact broke to the relay before any seal
  check ("preserve native compaction's existing passthrough"): a compact
  whose input carries a compaction magpie recorded the writer of went to
  Codex's own sign-in as it came, and a seal of another account's is
  refused there, its reason unread. The same request on /responses has
  gone through routing since bf931f82, where checkpointReaders holds it
  to the writer and checkpointError says why it can't be asked. The
  compact now gets the same refusal at its passthrough: checkpointOf on
  the body, and when the writer is not the sign-in auth.json here names
  (codexSealedRelayGone), 400 checkpointError instead of the relay. The
  sign-in's own seal relays as it came — the backend takes its own — and
  so does a seal a magpie key's candidate wrote, and any request whose
  chatgpt-account-id names an account other than auth.json's (a Codex
  signing from WSL or another CODEX_HOME signs with its own, which
  magpie's auth.json doesn't name — codexServed's caution): neither is
  judged here. /responses/compact still compacts natively as it came,
  unrecorded, when no recorded seal is on it.
- docs/subsystems/gateway-routing.md says so beside codexSealedFor.

Tests (fake ChatGPT backend, sandbox HOME, nothing on the network):
TestNativeCompactionCompactHoldsTheWriter, three subtests:
- another account's seal: 400 with the writer named, the way on, and
  "Native compaction is on for codex"; the backend asked 0 times.
- the sign-in's own seal: relayed, 200, the backend asked once.
- a request naming another account than auth.json's: relayed, 200.

Red and ablation, at upstream/main 04e8aa8f (this change's base):
- The test alone, codex_backend.go back to the base: the first subtest
  went red — 200, the backend asked /backend-api/codex/responses/compact
  with the seal on it. Restored: all three green. The ablation state is
  the baseline state (the change is one product file).
- go test -tags nogui -p 2 -count=1 -run 'NativeCompaction|Compact|
  Checkpoint|TestCodex' ./internal/gateway/: ok, 24s. -race on the new
  test and its seal siblings: ok.
- gofmt -l internal/gateway/: clean. go vet -tags nogui
  ./internal/gateway/ on darwin, GOOS=linux, GOOS=windows: clean.
  Three-platform go build -tags nogui ./...: ok, with the known
  trayimage cgo warning (darwin).
Not tried: a real ChatGPT backend, and whether its refusal of a seal is
the same on the legacy endpoint as on /responses (no real accounts; the
refusal is magpie's own either way).

Fixes #2642's legacy endpoint, reported by its reporter on /responses.

